WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.500
AR-15 Gas System 

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:06.297
As the expanding gases propel the&nbsp;
bullet down the barrel,

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:08.929
 a portion escapes through the gas port.

00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:12.855
This high pressure gas quickly&nbsp;
travels through the gas tube,

00:00:12.855 --> 00:00:16.423
leading to a chamber between the bolt and the carrier.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.903
The dwell&nbsp;time is the time the bullet spends
between the gas&nbsp;port and the muzzle.

00:00:22.903 --> 00:00:28.214
The pressure from the gas&nbsp;trapped behind the bullet
is necessary to cycle&nbsp;the rifle.

00:00:28.574 --> 00:00:32.645
The chamber between the bolt and carrier&nbsp;
acts as a pneumatic cylinder.

00:00:32.645 --> 00:00:37.605
Since the bolt cannot&nbsp;move forward,
the pressure forces the carrier&nbsp;to the rear.

00:00:37.605 --> 00:00:40.986
As the bullet clears the muzzle, the&nbsp;pressure drops

00:00:40.986 --> 00:00:45.708
and at this point the carrier has&nbsp;
picked up enough inertia to retract the bolt.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.626
The two vents on the carrier
pass over the gas rings&nbsp;on the bolt

00:00:49.626 --> 00:00:51.831
releasing the gases from the chamber.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.265
The bolt carrier continues to the rear&nbsp;
as it extracts the empty shell case.

